Subject: [PATCH] media: mediatek: add ISP Pass 1 and seninf drivers for MT8183

Port of the MediaTek camera stack from the ChromeOS 6.6 kernel
(drivers/media/platform/mediatek/isp/isp_50). The upstream attempt
stalled at RFC v7 in 2020, so mainline has no CSI-2 receiver or ISP
driver for these SoCs and the cameras on Kukui Chromebooks do not work.

seninf is the MIPI CSI-2 host; cam is ISP Pass 1, which writes Bayer
data and 3A statistics to memory. Demosaicing is left to userspace
(libcamera software ISP) since the DIP block is not ported.

Changes from the 6.6 sources are limited to API updates:
  - v4l2_subdev_get_try_format -> v4l2_subdev_state_get_format
  - platform driver .remove now returns void
  - v4l2_async_nf_parse_fwnode_endpoints replaced by an explicit
    fwnode_graph_for_each_endpoint loop
  - pad flags must be set before media_entity_pads_init
  - zero-initialise struct v4l2_subdev_format before get_fmt

Additionally the driver now supports streaming without the Request API,
reports V4L2_CAP_IO_MC and media bus code filtering, and exposes the
standard Bayer fourccs alongside the MediaTek ones, which lets
libcamera drive it through the simple pipeline handler.

